    "title": "Why Aldi execs overhauled their private-label brand strategy - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Mitchell Parton ,\n20 days ago Aldi has reimagined its branding and packaging to put its logo or endorsement on every private-label product in its stores. Previously, there were about 90 different brand names for Aldi’s private-label products, which make up more than 90% of the grocer’s selection. Now, the company is down to around 26-28 brands, and Aldi exclusives will now either carry the Aldi brand or retain other brand names such as Clancy’s, Simply Nature or Specially Selected but with the tagline “an Aldi Original.” Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
